ated and seed at startup only when the database is empty, and skip this when the app is run to generate the OpenAPI document\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"After the member cancels a booking or leaves a waitlist, can they book or join the same class again? If so, does that create a new booking row?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Yes. Cancelled rows don't count for already_booked, and a new row is created\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should promotion notices (listed until acknowledged) be stored?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fields on the booking (promoted-at and notice-acknowledged)\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How much sample data should be seeded, and what dates should it use? The request says 'a few rows', but §4.3 asks for 40+ sessions over the current and next week, including full, almost-full and cancelled classes and the demo member's bookings.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Seed only a few rows (a handful of sessions plus the demo member's bookings), relative to the day the database is created\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-1\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"The contract's server URL is /api and its paths are /me, /bookings and so on. Where should the endpoints actually answer, while the generated OpenAPI document still matches the contract? → assumed: Map the paths exactly as written (/me, …), add UsePathBase(\\\"/api\\\") so /api/me also works, and declare server /api in the generated document\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-2\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What should happen to the existing GET / route that returns \\\"API is up\\\"? → assumed: Keep it as it is, excluded from the OpenAPI document\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"data-migration\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-3\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How much sample data should the seed contain? The run instruction asks for 'a few rows'; §4.3 of the request asks for at least 40 sessions over two weeks. → assumed: No; the system starts empty, with seed data for set-up.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-4\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Should seed session times be fixed dates, or calculated from the date the database is created? The booking window and the 'past' rules depend on the current time. → assumed: Calculate them relative to the current week at the time of seeding, in Europe/London\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-5\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"If the demo member is promoted from a waitlist but the promotion would overlap another Booked class or go over the 10-booking limit, what should happen? → assumed: Promote anyway, because promotion is automatic\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-6\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the rule numbers (7 days, 15 minutes, 2 hours, 5-second undo, limit of 10) and the demo member's identity be code constants or configuration? → assumed: Code constants\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-7\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Which timezone and boundaries apply to 'today', week, month, streak and the timeOfDay filter? In particular, is a class starting at exactly 12:00 or 17:00 Morning, Afternoon or Evening? → assumed: Europe/London for everything; Morning < 12:00, Afternoon 12:00–16:59, Evening ≥ 17:00\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-8\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should duplicate Book taps be prevented from creating duplicate bookings? → assumed: Check already_booked inside the same database transaction before inserting\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-9\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should this run add the automated business-rule tests from §10, and how is the clock controlled in those tests? → assumed: Add rule tests in App.Tests through WebApplicationFactory, with time injected using .NET's TimeProvider; the end-to-end test belongs to the web repo\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-10\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"The contract's description says it is served in the browser over local storage, but this run uses SQLite. Should that description text change? → assumed: Leave the locked contract untouched\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-11\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"The contract's server URL is /api, and its paths are written without that prefix (/me, /bookings, …). Where should the endpoints be mapped? → assumed: Map them under an /api route group (GET /api/me), so the paths in the built document still match the contract\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-12\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"What should happen to the existing GET / route that returns \\\"API is up\\\"? → assumed: Keep it, still left out of the OpenAPI document\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-13\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the rule numbers be constants in code or configuration? These are: the limit of 10 bookings, the 7-day and 15-minute booking window, the 2-hour late cancel, the 5-second undo and the Europe/London timezone. → assumed: Constants in code\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-14\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"How should the time rules get the current time, so that tests can check the windows (7 days, 15 minutes, 2 hours, 5-second undo)? → assumed: Inject TimeProvider (system clock by default), so tests can substitute a fake clock\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-15\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"The demo member is first on a waitlist. If promoting them would break the overlap rule or the limit of 10, what should promotion do? → assumed: Promote anyway (promotion is not a new booking request)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-16\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Duplicate taps on Book must not create duplicate bookings. How strong does that guarantee need to be? → assumed: Rely on the already_booked check inside the same request (there is one member, so no extra machinery)\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-17\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"If a database read or write fails, or another exception is not handled, what should the API return? → assumed: The contract's Error body with code storage_failure and a plain message, and no stack trace, using the status the contract declares\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 13,\n     \"lineStart\": 9,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"var app = builder.Build();\\napp.UseCors();\\napp.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n\\napp.Run();\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-1\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"None of the contract's operations exist in the API today. Program.cs maps a single route: GET \\\"/\\\", which returns \\\"API is up\\\" and is left out of the OpenAPI description. There are no endpoints for /me, /schedule, /sessions/{sessionId}, /bookings, /waitlist, /me/bookings, /me/stats, /me/promotion-notices or the /test simulate hook.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 10,\n     \"lineStart\": 1,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"openapi: 3.0.3\\ninfo:\\n  title: Pulse Studio Booking API\\n  version: 1.0.0\\n  description: >-\\n    Contract for the Pulse Studio class booking app. In this release it is served\\n    inside the browser by the booking service over local storage (no network);\\n    the web app calls it only through the generated client in lib/api.\\nservers:\\n  - url: /api\",\n     \"symbol\": \"info/servers\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 19,\n     \"lineStart\": 17,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"  /me:\\n    get:\\n      operationId: getMember\",\n     \"symbol\": \"getMember\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 39,\n     \"lineStart\": 36,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"  /schedule:\\n    get:\\n      operationId: getSchedule\\n      tags: [schedule]\",\n     \"symbol\": \"getSchedule\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 240,\n     \"lineStart\": 238,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"  /bookings:\\n    post:\\n      operationId: createBooking\",\n     \"symbol\": \"createBooking\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 655,\n     \"lineStart\": 653,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"  /test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation:\\n    post:\\n      operationId: simulateOtherMemberCancellation\",\n     \"symbol\": \"simulateOtherMemberCancellation\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-2\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The locked contract (contracts/openapi.yaml, OpenAPI 3.0.3, 'Pulse Studio Booking API') has server base url /api and 13 operations: getMember GET /me, getSchedule GET /schedule (array query filters date/type/intensity/timeOfDay), getSession GET /sessions/{sessionId}, createBooking POST /bookings, undoBooking POST /bookings/{bookingId}/undo, cancelBooking POST /bookings/{bookingId}/cancel, joinWaitlist POST /waitlist, leaveWaitlist POST /bookings/{bookingId}/leave-waitlist, getMyBookings GET /me/bookings, getStats GET /me/stats, listPromotionNotices GET /me/promotion-notices, acknowledgePromotionNotices POST /me/promotion-notices/acknowledge (204), and simulateOtherMemberCancellation POST /test/sessions/{sessionId}/simulate-other-member-cancellation. Its description says it is served inside the browser over local storage. That conflicts with the SQLite part of the request.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 996,\n     \"lineStart\": 982,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"    Error:\\n      type: object\\n      required: [code, message]\\n      properties:\\n        code:\\n          type: string\\n          enum: [already_booked, class_full, not_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio, overlap, limit_reached, invalid_booking_state, undo_expired, not_found, invalid_request, storage_failure]\\n        message:\\n          type: string\\n          description: Plain-language message safe to show to the member\\n        session:\\n          nullable: true\\n          description: Refreshed session, sent with class_full so the screen can switch to Join waitlist\\n          allOf:\\n            - $ref: \\\"#/components/schemas/Session\\\"\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Error\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 817,\n     \"lineStart\": 815,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"    Session:\\n      type: object\\n      required: [id, name, type, intensity, instructor, room, startsAt, endsAt, durationMin, capacity, bookedCount, waitlistCount, description, whatToBring, status, availabilityLabel, capacityLabel, actionState, myBookingId]\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Session\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-3\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-3\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The contract defines the response shapes and a fixed Error code enum. These must be matched exactly: Session (with actionState, availabilityLabel, capacityLabel, myBookingId), Booking, BookingChange, MyBookings, Stats, PromotionNotices and SimulationResult. The Error code enum is already_booked, class_full, not_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio, overlap, limit_reached, invalid_booking_state, undo_expired, not_found, invalid_request and storage_failure. The error's session field is a refreshed session, sent with class_full.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 8,\n     \"lineStart\": 6,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/App.Api.csproj\",\n     \"quote\": \"    <!-- the build writes the API's OpenAPI document here; the factory compares it with contracts/openapi.yaml -->\\n    <OpenApiDocumentsDirectory>$(MSBuildProjectDirectory)/openapi</OpenApiDocumentsDirectory>\\n    <OpenApiGenerateDocumentsOptions>--file-name built</OpenApiGenerateDocumentsOptions>\",\n     \"symbol\": \"App.Api.csproj\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 6,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"builder.Services.AddOpenApi();\\n// a local file database; nothing touches it at startup (the build runs this file to write the API's OpenAPI document)\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-4\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The build checks contract conformance: it writes the generated OpenAPI document to App.Api/openapi (file name 'built'), and the factory compares it with contracts/openapi.yaml. AddOpenApi() is registered in Program.cs. The startup comment says nothing touches the database at startup, because the build runs Program.cs to generate the document.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 7,\n     \"lineStart\": 7,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"builder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDb>(o => o.UseSqlite(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\\\"App\\\") ?? \\\"Data Source=app.db\\\"));\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 7,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/AppDb.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\\n{\\n}\",\n     \"symbol\": \"AppDb\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 15,\n     \"lineStart\": 15,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/App.Api.csproj\",\n     \"quote\": \"    <PackageReference Include=\\\"Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite\\\" Version=\\\"9.0.0\\\" />\",\n     \"symbol\": \"App.Api.csproj\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-5\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-2\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"SQLite is wired up but holds nothing. AppDb is registered with UseSqlite, using connection string 'App' or the default 'Data Source=app.db'. The EF Core Sqlite 9.0.0 package is referenced. AppDb is an empty DbContext with no DbSets, entity configuration or seed data (HasData), and nothing calls EnsureCreated or migrations. No search turned up any seed code, migrations or connection-string config.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 286,\n     \"lineStart\": 285,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"        \\\"409\\\":\\n          description: Rejected by a booking rule (already_booked, class_full, outside_booking_window, class_has_started, cancelled_by_studio, overlap, limit_reached)\",\n     \"symbol\": \"createBooking\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 301,\n     \"lineStart\": 301,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"      summary: Undo a booking within 5 seconds, as if it was never made\",\n     \"symbol\": \"undoBooking\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"line